  "title": "Emotional Development and Big Feelings",
  "content": "Children experience emotions intensely because their regulation systems are still developing. They rely on adults to help them calm down, understand their feelings, and learn healthy coping strategies. When parents respond with patience and empathy, children learn that emotions are safe and manageable.\n\nMany challenging behaviours—tantrums, crying, shutting down—are signs that a child is overwhelmed, not misbehaving. Emotional development takes time, and children need repeated support to build these skills.\n\nThis lesson explores how parents can become emotional coaches, helping children name feelings, express themselves safely, and recover from difficult moments.",
